  "Show more headlines": "显示更多标题",
  "How headlines are filed and scored": "标题如何归类和评分",
  "Filing.": "归类。",
  "A headline is filed under a stock only when it names the company or its ticker. Words that could mean something else (“apple”, “shell”, “reliance”) also need a market word nearby, such as “shares” or “earnings”. Open Why? on any headline to see exactly which words filed it.": "只有当标题提到公司名称或股票代码时，才会归入该股票。可能有其他含义的词（“apple”“shell”“reliance”）还需要附近出现市场相关词，例如“shares”或“earnings”。在任意标题上打开“为什么？”可查看具体是哪些词让它被归类。",
  "Tone.": "情绪。",
  "Each headline is checked against a fixed list of positive and negative finance words (“beats”, “upgrade”, “plunges”, “lawsuit”…). More positive words than negative makes it positive, and the other way round makes it negative. “Not” in front of a word flips it, and questions are not counted. It is a count of words, not a prediction.": "每条标题都会与一份固定的正面和负面金融词汇表比对（“beats”“upgrade”“plunges”“lawsuit”…）。正面词多于负面词即为正面，反之为负面。词前的“not”会反转其含义，问句不计入。这是词数统计，不是预测。",
  "Order.": "排序。",
  "Stocks are listed by how much was written about them, never by how positive the news was, so the page never reads as a ranking of what to buy. A stock with no headlines shows “none”, which is not the same as neutral news.": "股票按被报道的多少排序，而不是按新闻有多正面排序，因此页面绝不会像一份买入排行榜。没有标题的股票显示“无”，这与中性新闻不同。",
  "The pond.": "池塘。",
  "Each stock is placed by its net tone: positive headlines minus negative ones, divided by all its headlines. Within ±0.10 it sits in the neutral zone. A stock with fewer than five headlines is faded, because a handful of headlines can swing it either way. Stocks with no headlines are left out. Where a stock sits describes the wording of its headlines, not the stock.": "每只股票按其净情绪放置：正面标题减去负面标题，再除以其全部标题。在 ±0.10 以内位于中性区。标题少于五条的股票会变淡，因为少量标题就可能让它偏向任一方。没有标题的股票不显示。股票所在位置描述的是其标题的措辞，而不是股票本身。",
  "Sources.": "来源。",
  "NewsAPI.org: the most recent hundred headlines from the last seven days, from a fixed list of financial publishers.": "NewsAPI.org：最近七天内来自固定财经媒体列表的最新一百条标题。",
